.page jobs 1 manage background jobs
.alias fg bg

# SYNOPSIS
*jobs*
*fg* [%_N_]
*bg* [%_N_]

# DESCRIPTION
These gapsh builtins deal with commands started with `&`. `jobs` lists the running jobs as `[N]  Running  COMMAND`. `fg` makes the most recent job (or job _N_) the foreground job and waits for it, returning its status. `bg` only prints the job: background jobs already run in the background, and a job cannot be stopped and resumed here.

# EXIT STATUS
1 if there is no such job.

# EXAMPLES
    sleep 100 &
    jobs
    fg %1

# SEE ALSO
wait(1), kill(1), ps(1)
